\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Detailed Description\par
\pard\plain 
{
\pard\plain \s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid {\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
CPP-API: Primary logging facility of {\b Assimp}. \par
}

{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
The library stores its primary {\b Logger} as a static member of this class. {\b get()} returns this primary logger. By default the underlying implementation is just a #NullLogger which rejects all log messages. By calling {\b create()}, logging is turned on. To capture the log output multiple log streams (#LogStream) can be attach to the logger. Some default streams for common streaming locations (such as a file, std::cout, OutputDebugString()) are also provided.\par
If you wish to customize the logging at an even deeper level supply your own implementation of {\b Logger} to {\b set()}. \par
{{\s5\sb90\sa30\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs16\cgrid 
Note\par}\pard\plain \s81\li360\widctlpar\ql\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {\s17 \sa60 \sb30
The whole logging stuff causes a small extra overhead for all imports. \par
}}}}
{\pard\widctlpar\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brsp20 \adjustright \par}
